What is Docker? 🐳

Docker is a popular tool/platform used to create, package, and run containers.

For your project:

College AI Assistant
        ↓
Dockerfile
        ↓
Docker builds the application
        ↓
Docker Image
        ↓
Docker Container

=====

Important difference

| Item                 | Meaning                                               |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| **Dockerfile**       | Instructions for building the application environment |
| **Docker Image**     | The packaged application template                     |
| **Docker Container** | A running instance of the image                       |
| **Docker**           | Tool used to build and run containers                 |


=======

Example

Your project:

college-ai-assistant/
│
├── main.py
├── requirements.txt
├── Dockerfile
├── templates/
└── static/

Your Dockerfile tells Docker something like:

Use Python
↓
Install FastAPI and dependencies
↓
Copy my project files
↓
Start the application

Then:

Dockerfile
    ↓
docker build
    ↓
Docker Image 📦
    ↓
docker run
    ↓
Running Container 🚀

=========
